Stage 3 / Phase 2 — bidirectionality verification log
======================================================

Purpose: for each production behavior family added this phase, prove the new
tests are genuine — they PASS against correct code, and FAIL (naming the new
tests, for the right reason) when the production behavior is deliberately
broken. Each family: capture PASS → break production (sed) → genuine vitest FAIL
→ restore (git checkout) → PASS.

Worktree: .worktrees/chained-p2 (branch feature/chained-p2).
Runner: vitest 4.1.10, node env (no jsdom). All -t filters scope to the new
Phase-2 rows only.


FAMILY 1 — graphToFlow emission (src/ui/graph-flow.ts)
------------------------------------------------------
Behavior: under-supply edge labels render the EXACT shortfall value.

PASS (baseline):
  $ npx vitest run src/ui/graph-flow.test.ts -t "graphToFlow"
        Tests  13 passed | 3 skipped (16)

BREAK: drop the shortfall value from the under-supply label —
  sed -i 's|label: `${itemName} · short ${formatRate(finding.shortfall)}/min`,|label: `${itemName} · short`,|' src/ui/graph-flow.ts

FAIL (broken, expected):
  $ npx vitest run src/ui/graph-flow.test.ts -t "graphToFlow — edges"
     × under-supply renders the exact shortfall
     × under-supply exact fractional shortfall (75/2 class)
   FAIL  … > under-supply renders the exact shortfall
   AssertionError: expected 'Iron Ingot · short' to be 'Iron Ingot · short 150/min'
   FAIL  … > under-supply exact fractional shortfall (75/2 class)
   AssertionError: expected 'Iron Ingot · short' to be 'Iron Ingot · short 37.5/min'
        Tests  2 failed | 5 passed | 9 skipped (16)

RESTORE: git checkout src/ui/graph-flow.ts → Tests 7 passed | 9 skipped (16)


